chat_messages.text:
Now I'm building out the four Blade views for the exam module, starting with the create form which needs dynamic question management using Alpine.js to handle adding and removing questions on the fly while maintaining the established design patterns with primary and accent colors.

For the create view, I'm setting up Alpine data to manage an array of questions where each question has a type, content, options for multiple choice, and a correct answer index. The form will use standard Laravel array naming conventions in the HTML inputs so the controller can validate and process them properly, with Alpine rendering the dynamic fields using x-for loops to bind the correct name attributes.

The index view will display a list of exams with status indicators showing whether each user hasn't started, is currently taking, or has completed the exam with a link to view details. The show view serves as the pre-start page displaying the exam title, description, duration, and question count, with a button to begin if not yet started or results information if already completed.

For the take view, I'm building the actual exam interface with anti-cheat measures like detecting when the user switches tabs or loses focus, auto-saving answers via fetch requests as they change, an optional timer based on the exam duration, and a submit button that finalizes the exam. Since essay questions require manual grading and we haven't built that UI yet, I'll keep it simple for now and note it as a future enhancement.Sekarang bikin ke-4 view-nya. Mulai dari yang paling sederhana ke yang paling kompleks.

